  "topology_summary": "Point-to-point single-twisted-pair full-duplex links for 100BASE-T1 / 1000BASE-T1 / 10BASE-T1L (one master PHY, one slave PHY per link, echo-cancelled bidirectional on the one pair), plus a MULTIDROP 'mixing segment' for 10BASE-T1S in which several PHYs share one short single-pair bus and use PLCA (Physical Layer Collision Avoidance, node 0 = coordinator) to take deterministic round-robin transmit opportunities. AVB / TSN can layer on top for time-sensitive traffic.",
  "package_summary": "The IEEE 802.3bw / 802.3bp / 802.3cg amendments define single-pair PHY (PMA/PCS/PMD) and management parameters added to IEEE 802.3; the MDI is one balanced twisted pair. Connectors, harness, and automotive EMC test are governed by the OPEN Alliance and OEM specifications, not by the IEEE amendments themselves.",
